  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A water drop of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> is broken into <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>729</mn></math> equal droplets. If surface tension of water is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>75</mn><mi>dyne</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, then the gain in surface energy upto first decimal place will be</p><p>[Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>14</mn></math>]</p>",
    "image": null
  },
